# In-app dialogs for HTTP actions

Never use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or `window.prompt` for anything tied to an API call, mutation, or user-facing HTTP result.

The browser box that says “hostname says …” (for example `hr.creativeintelligent.ae says`) is a bug, not an acceptable pattern.

## Required pattern

- Confirmations before create, update, delete, assign, or other mutations use the shared `ConfirmDialog` in `apps/web/src/components/ui/confirm-dialog.tsx`.
- API errors stay in-app: inline on the form or page, or the same modal style. Never a native dialog.
- Destructive actions use `variant="destructive"` on `ConfirmDialog`.

## Do not

```tsx
window.confirm(`Delete “${name}”?`);
alert(err.message);
```

## Do

```tsx
<ConfirmDialog
  open={Boolean(pending)}
  title={`Delete “${pending?.name}”?`}
  description="This cannot be undone."
  confirmLabel="Delete"
  variant="destructive"
  busy={busy}
  onConfirm={confirmDelete}
  onOpenChange={(open) => { if (!open && !busy) setPending(null); }}
/>
```
